    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-yakuba-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 2.157 µm on the D. yakuba abdominal cuticle (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 88.9/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 closes both pass-1 remediation items. The reported nonlinear wavelength is the isotropic FFT ring, 1.993 µm, against the linear λ* of 2.157 µm (about 8% short, not set equal). Radial arm spacing averages 12.25 lattice px against λ* = 12.91 px, KS = 0.328, down from the bead-spacing KS of 0.592. Dispersion r remains 0.995. CV similarity of the 12-frame 640×480 GIF against the specimen is 86.8. Overall clears the pass-2 gate. A no-flux boundary would remove the edge beads; that is not required to state the wavelength. Overall 88.9/100 (faithfulness 88.4, reproducibility 90.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 1d40797a1aa1c46f0b61e38c4454905b1b892739; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, scipy 1.18.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_yakuba_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-yakuba-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 1d40797a1aa1c46f0b61e38c4454905b1b892739, image/png, 453541 B, 1248×960 px, artifact_sha256 5b349030a42551dc891b113c913f5633a1bdb089905cd189149489f0302eb3e2 (sha256 5b349030a42551dc891b113c913f5633a1bdb089905cd189149489f0302eb3e2), spec_fingerprint 92972fdde4bae9de4e9a6818d7f399847640e9a945f2f00a3077f1693c946f83. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 92972fdde4bae9de4e9a6818d7f399847640e9a945f2f00a3077f1693c946f83; artifact_sha256: 012a50ed1719b0b98fa95bbf04722cbf783e8f81f6c0fb6e8516a2e59886f126; input_dataset_sha256: {drosophila_yakuba_specimen.jpg=71ea43a85af08357...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-yakuba-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a finite wavenumber. Schnakenberg (1979) supplies the kinetics. Carbone et al. (2005), Llopart et al. (2002) and Wittkopp et al. (2002) supply the yakuba pigmentation biology and the Yellow/Ebony antagonism.; reconstructed_in_script: Discrete dispersion test (r = 0.995), equal-diffusion ablation (σ* = −0.102), monotone D_v sweep, and a spiral Schnakenberg integration whose FFT ring is the reported wavelength. | Radial arm-to-arm periods replace the pass-1 bead nearest-neighbour distance. The bead KS (0.592) is kept only as ks_pass1_nearest_neighbour.; transfer_boundary: Periodic boundaries still bead the spiral where it meets the opposite edge. Ratio statistics cross to the specimen; pixel bin indices do not, because the specimen is 800×600 and the GIF is 640×480.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a measured 2.2 µm granule spacing in Carbone et al. The 2.157 µm figure is the selected wavelength of this reconstruction. | Does not claim the gallery JPEG is a light micrograph of yakuba cuticle. It is the project species-gallery canonical asset, SHA-256 pinned. | No successor chronospecies. The only comparison is to D. willistoni at 86 µm (ratio 40.01).." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.89e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-yakuba-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 2.157 µm on the D. yakuba abdominal cuticle (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Raising D_v from 10 to 40 lengthens λ* monotonically (1.86, 2.00, 2.16, 2.32, 2.50 µm). The reference row D_v = 20 is the 2.157 µm phenomenon. Spiral arm count is fixed at 3 so the sweep is not confounded with it." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-yakuba-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-yakuba-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

