    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-yakuba-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 2.157 µm on the D. yakuba abdominal cuticle (Holocene, 0 Ma) (Drosophila yakuba)",
        "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 2.157 µm on the D. yakuba abdominal cuticle (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Drosophila yakuba morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-yakuba-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-yakuba-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-yakuba-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-yakuba-turing-wavelength-s0-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-yakuba-turing-wavelength-s0-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-yakuba-turing-wavelength-s0.py, datasets/drosophila_yakuba_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_yakuba_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json, morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3212_drosophila_yakuba_turing_wavelength_s0.lean implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila yakuba specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/drosophila_yakuba_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_yakuba_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-yakuba-turing-wavelength-s0.py>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3212_drosophila_yakuba_turing_wavelength_s0.lean> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila yakuba" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim a measured 2.2 µm granule spacing in Carbone et al. The 2.157 µm figure is the selected wavelength of this reconstruction.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the gallery JPEG is a light micrograph of yakuba cuticle. It is the project species-gallery canonical asset, SHA-256 pinned.",
        "does_not_claim: No successor chronospecies. The only comparison is to D. willistoni at 86 µm (ratio 40.01).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Discrete dispersion test (r = 0.995), equal-diffusion ablation (σ* = −0.102), monotone D_v sweep, and a spiral Schnakenberg integration whose FFT ring is the reported wavelength.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Radial arm-to-arm periods replace the pass-1 bead nearest-neighbour distance. The bead KS (0.592) is kept only as ks_pass1_nearest_neighbour.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a finite wavenumber. Schnakenberg (1979) supplies the kinetics. Carbone et al. (2005), Llopart et al. (2002) and Wittkopp et al. (2002) supply the yakuba pigmentation biology and the Yellow/Ebony antagonism.",
        "transfer_boundary: Periodic boundaries still bead the spiral where it meets the opposite edge. Ratio statistics cross to the specimen; pixel bin indices do not, because the specimen is 800×600 and the GIF is 640×480." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila yakuba (Afrotropical Savanna Fruit Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
