    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-yakuba-turing-wavelength-s0.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/drosophila_yakuba_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_yakuba_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3212_drosophila_yakuba_turing_wavelength_s0.lean; output: docs/media/drosophila_yakuba_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila yakuba; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, scipy 1.18.1; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a finite wavenumber. Schnakenberg (1979) supplies the kinetics. Carbone et al. (2005), Llopart et al. (2002) and Wittkopp et al. (2002) supply the yakuba pigmentation biology and the Yellow/Ebony antagonism.; reconstructed_in_script: Discrete dispersion test (r = 0.995), equal-diffusion ablation (σ* = −0.102), monotone D_v sweep, and a spiral Schnakenberg integration whose FFT ring is the reported wavelength. | Radial arm-to-arm periods replace the pass-1 bead nearest-neighbour distance. The bead KS (0.592) is kept only as ks_pass1_nearest_neighbour.; transfer_boundary: Periodic boundaries still bead the spiral where it meets the opposite edge. Ratio statistics cross to the specimen; pixel bin indices do not, because the specimen is 800×600 and the GIF is 640×480.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a measured 2.2 µm granule spacing in Carbone et al. The 2.157 µm figure is the selected wavelength of this reconstruction. | Does not claim the gallery JPEG is a light micrograph of yakuba cuticle. It is the project species-gallery canonical asset, SHA-256 pinned. | No successor chronospecies. The only comparison is to D. willistoni at 86 µm (ratio 40.01).]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
